{title: Not From Works}
{subtitle: Ephesians 2:4–10; 2 Corinthians 12:7–10}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Ebmaj7] |
| [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I kept a ledger in my [Dm7]head of every wrong and right
Counting up my better days and lying a[Bb]wake at night
Thought that I could earn a [Dm7]place if I just tried some more
[Ebmaj7]Pay a debt I couldn't pay and knock on heaven's [Bb]door
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But God, who is rich in mer[Dm7]cy, found me dead in all my [Ebmaj7]sin
Because of the great love he had, he made me live again
[Bb]He made me alive togeth[Dm7]er with Christ, though I had noth[Ebmaj7]ing to bring
And raised me up and seated me with him beside the [Bb]King
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
By grace you have [Dm7]been saved [Ebmaj7]through faith
And this is not from your[Bb]selves
It is the [Dm7]gift of [Ebmaj7]God
Not from works, so that no one may [Bb]boast
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
There's a thorn I've carried [Dm7]and I begged him, take it a[Ebmaj7]way
Three times I pleaded with the Lord, three times I knelt to pray
[Bb]But he did not re[Dm7]move it, and he gave a better [Ebmaj7]word
The truest answer to a prayer that I have ever heard
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]My grace is [Dm7]enough for you
For [Ebmaj7]my power is brought to [Gm7]its fullness in weakness
[Cm7]When I am [Dm7]weak, then [Ebmaj7]I am strong
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]By grace you have been [Dm7]saved through [Ebmaj7]faith
And this is not from your[Bb]selves
It is the [Dm7]gift of [Ebmaj7]God
Not from works, so that no one may [Bb]boast
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
It is the [Dm7]gift of [Ebmaj7]God
Grace, only [Bb]grace [Dm7][Ebmaj7]
{end_of_verse}
